If you change your mind about a command, backspace to the start and hit RETURN.
This is guaranteed to restore the status quo. When editing, the screen is      
divided by a vertical line in the first column of the right screen as a guide  
to the screen boundaries. This line can be overwritten, and is not saved  spaces in the text. Other displays are available via the SEE command,
but these are for information only. The attribute display (SEE PRESTEL) is the 
only one that can be edited.                                                   
                      on    
disc when writing out a file. The cursor will be placed initially at the top   
left of the screen.                                                            
                                                                               
To co                                                         
Right screen displays show a dot wherever there is a visible but non-relevant  
character, e.g. an alphanumeric character after SEE GRAPHIC. In the PRESTEL    
attribute display these dots mark anstruct a page of text, simply type it onto the left half of the screen.  
The RETURN and cursor keys will behave exactly as normal, except that column 40
will be treated as the right hand margin. Page layout can be tidied up with the
CTRL-N,S,E and W cll the visible characters on the left screen
i.e. all but spaces and attribute control characters. New attribute control    
characters must be typed between the dots - either on top of spaces or existing
control characters. Cursor keys are active on thommands to move the text about. If you want to use colours   
other than black-on-white, or special attributes such as double height, a SPACE
must be entered on the left screen at the required position, as the attribute  
cannot be placed in a position e right screen half, but other-
wise only characters from the special set shown on the next frame (8.5) are    
recognised. When an attribute is typed, the cursor does not move - when you    
see the effect you may wish to undo what you just did...!    currently occupied by a character. To edit an   
existing page, READ the file and then type over the sections that you wish to  
change.                                                                        
