Character set for PRESTEL attribute controls:                                  
                                                                               
   W R G B M C Y   set alp--
When the text is complete, change screens using CTRL-P and enter any special   
attribute characters on the right screen. After a READ command, the right half 
of the screen will be showing the attribute control characters which normally  
appear ashanumeric mode and colour: white, red, green, blue,  
                   magenta, cyan, yellow.                                      
   w r g b m c y   set mosaic (graphic) mode and colour.                       
                                                                               
       *  :        set contiguous/separated mosaics.                           
       !  =        hold/release mosaic.                                        
       f  s        flashing/steady.                           
Any double height attribute causes the whole of the next line to be obscured,  
except for the lower halves of double height characters. The next line will    
remain in the screen buffer and will reappear if all double height attribute   
c                           
       1  2        set normal/double height. Any double height characters will 
                   cause the whole of the next line to be obscured.            
       h           conceal display ("hidden"). Any "set mode & coontrol characters are deleted from the line above. The WRITE command will only
output those characters visible on the screen at the time of writing.          
                                                                               
Note also thatlour"         
                   control cancels this code.                                  
       +           set background colour (to current alpha or mosaic colour).  
       -           set black background.                                       the cursor cannot be placed on the lower half of a double       
height line in either screen half.                                             
